  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Senegalese carry a Muslim first name (Mamadou, Cheikh, Fatou, Aminata) and a family name (sant) from the father's line, which also tells people where a family comes from: Diop, Ndiaye, Fall and Gueye are Wolof; Faye, Sarr and Diouf are Serer; Diallo, Ba and Sow are Pulaar; Diatta and Sagna are Diola. Serer and Diola families include many Catholics with French saints' names. Women keep their own family name after marriage. Ndèye and Mame are often joined to a first name (Ndèye Fatou, Mame Diarra), and men named after a respected elder are often called by a nickname such as Pape, Mbaye or Modou.",
